    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Fish need oxygen, just like us! But they get it from the water, not the air.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "You",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "From air",
              "icon": "💨",
              "cue": "air"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Fish",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "From water",
              "icon": "💧",
              "cue": "water"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "There's oxygen in water?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes, a little bit of oxygen is mixed into water, too small to see. Fish have special parts to catch it, called gills!",
      "punch": "gills",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐟",
        "text": "Fish have gills!",
        "cue": "gills",
        "sub": "Oxygen is in water",
        "sub_cue": "oxygen"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Where are the gills?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "On each side of a fish's head, under little flaps. They look like soft, red feathers.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Animals/Servier/fish-1",
        "text": "Soft, red and feathery",
        "cue": "feathers",
        "sub": "Under little flaps",
        "sub_cue": "flaps"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How do they work?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The fish gulps water into its mouth and pushes it over its gills. The gills grab the oxygen, and the water flows out the sides.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Water's trip",
        "traveler": "💧",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "👄",
            "label": "Into mouth",
            "cue": "mouth"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🐟",
            "label": "Over gills",
            "cue": "pushes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Oxygen grabbed",
            "cue": "grab"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌊",
            "label": "Out the sides",
            "cue": "flows"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Can a fish breathe air, like me?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Most fish can't. Gills are made to work in water, so fish are happiest swimming in it!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐠",
        "text": "Gills work in water",
        "cue": "gills",
        "sub": "Happy swimming!",
        "sub_cue": "swimming"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What about whales and dolphins? They swim in water too!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐋",
        "text": "Whales and dolphins?",
        "cue": "whales"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Surprise! Whales and dolphins aren't fish. They have lungs like us, so they swim up to the top to breathe air.",
      "punch": "surprise",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Not fish!",
